This is only because system_clock is in nanoseconds and a signed 64-bit count. 

"The value of std::chrono::system_clock::time_point::max() represents the maximum representable time point for the system clock. This value is implementation-defined because the C++ standard does not mandate a specific precision or epoch for system_clock." - Google AI overview 

It is kind of like asking for the largest possible value of an int.. 

I think we are okay, we have a narrow linux toolchain but did want to call this out.

